oox: the PPTX import leaves the undo lock balanced

DrawDocShell disables undo while a file loads, so PowerPointImport's
isLocked() is true and it notes the manager as locked; it still calls
lock() but never unlock(). The helper's lock count stays at one after
the load, while the shell turns undo back on directly. Every later
XUndoManager::lock() then only counts and leaves undo on: the PPTX
export's own lock does nothing, and each layout's temporary slide is
recorded as "Delete slides". A deck with six layouts gained six steps
on every PPTX save, and the next undo put a stray slide into it (Ely:
one undo after a recovery snapshot of t.pptx gave 10 slides for 9).
Import and export now lock only what they unlock.
--- a/oox/source/ppt/pptimport.cxx
+++ b/oox/source/ppt/pptimport.cxx
@@ -95,7 +95,9 @@
         if(xUndoManager.is())
         {
             bWasUnLocked = !xUndoManager->isLocked();
-            xUndoManager->lock();
+            // Ely: unlocked only if locked here; else locks stay.
+            if (bWasUnLocked)
+                xUndoManager->lock();
         }
     }
 
@@ -237,7 +239,8 @@
                 if (xUndoManager.is())
                 {
                     bWasUnLocked = !xUndoManager->isLocked();
-                    xUndoManager->lock();
+                    if (bWasUnLocked)
+                        xUndoManager->lock();
                 }
             }
             comphelper::ScopeGuard aGuard([xUndoManager, bWasUnLocked] {
